  (73454, 191, 'But it does have a message.', 1029.942, 1031.777, NULL),
  (73455, 191, 'This is the whole shooting match.', 1031.819, 1033.988, NULL),
  (73456, 191, 'Anybody here without kids,
ask someone with kids.', 1034.029, 1037.366, NULL),
  (73457, 191, 'You have your world of work,', 1037.408, 1038.784, NULL),
  (73458, 191, 'you have your world of friends,
you have your world of kids.', 1038.784, 1041.620, NULL),
  (73459, 191, 'Something happens here, your whole
world shrinks to this.', 1041.620, 1045.583, NULL),
  (73460, 191, '(Applause)', 1049.086, 1055.384, NULL),
  (73461, 191, 'So I present, as I wrap here,
with just a few questions.', 1055.426, 1058.846, NULL),
  (73462, 191, 'One,', 1058.887, 1060.139, NULL),
  (73463, 191, 'if you acknowledge that our kids
are the most important thing in our lives,', 1060.139, 1063.726, NULL),
  (73464, 191, 'that everything else
we do here is meaningful,', 1063.767, 1065.936, NULL),
  (73465, 191, 'but our kids'' well-being
and prosperity is profound.', 1065.936, 1068.397, NULL),
  (73466, 191, 'If you acknowledge
that they''re doing more poorly', 1068.439, 1071.525, NULL),
  (73467, 191, 'than previous generations.', 1071.567, 1073.569, NULL),
  (73468, 191, 'If you believe there’s a chance', 1073.569, 1075.154, NULL),
  (73469, 191, 'that the illusion of complexity
has done nothing but provide cloud cover', 1075.154, 1078.657, NULL),
  (73470, 191, 'for the unbelievable
transfer of good will,', 1078.699, 1081.619, NULL),
  (73471, 191, 'of well-being and of prosperity
from young to old.', 1081.660, 1085.205, NULL),
  (73472, 191, 'And if you believe we can
actually fix these problems', 1085.247, 1087.750, NULL),
  (73473, 191, 'and we have the resources,', 1087.791, 1089.543, NULL),
  (73474, 191, 'then I present to you, I posit,', 1089.543, 1092.004, NULL),
  (73475, 191, 'I augur the question that I hope
has more veracity', 1092.046, 1095.215, NULL),
  (73476, 191, 'than it did 17 minutes
and 24 seconds ago.', 1095.215, 1098.927, NULL),
  (73477, 191, 'And that''s the following question.', 1099.261, 1101.555, NULL),
  (73478, 191, 'Do we love our children?', 1104.016, 1105.851, NULL),
  (73479, 191, 'My name is Scott Galloway,', 1107.061, 1108.395, NULL),
  (73480, 191, 'I teach at NYU,
and I appreciate your time.', 1108.437, 1110.481, NULL),
  (73481, 191, '(Cheers and applause)', 1110.522, 1113.692, NULL),
  (73482, 191, 'Thank you.', 1113.734, 1114.902, NULL),
  (73483, 191, '(Applause)', 1114.943, 1116.612, NULL),
  (73484, 192, 'So when I think about confidence,
I first ground myself in the definition.', 4.167, 8.713, NULL),
  (73485, 192, 'Confidence is just the reliance', 8.755, 10.840, NULL),
  (73486, 192, 'or assurance that we believe
in someone''s abilities or qualities.', 10.882, 16.346, NULL),
  (73487, 192, 'But how do we know
someone''s abilities or qualities?', 16.388, 18.890, NULL),
  (73488, 192, 'How does anyone believe in mine?', 18.932, 21.309, NULL),
  (73489, 192, 'It''s simply through actions.', 21.351, 23.353, NULL),
  (73490, 192, 'So the best way
to drive and build confidence,', 23.395, 25.564, NULL),
  (73491, 192, 'whether we’re looking to hone it
or build a reputation for it', 25.564, 28.900, NULL),
  (73492, 192, 'or encourage people to have it in us,  ', 28.900, 32.153, NULL),
  (73493, 192, 'is to drive action.', 32.153, 34.155, NULL),
  (73494, 192, 'Interestingly, many people
think you need a lot of confidence', 34.155, 37.158, NULL),
  (73495, 192, 'to take bold action.', 37.158, 38.868, NULL),
  (73496, 192, 'I think the opposite is true.', 38.868, 40.745, NULL),
  (73497, 192, 'It’s action. Just getting
comfortable with it over time.', 40.745, 43.873, NULL),
  (73498, 192, 'Doing more and better regularly.', 43.915, 46.084, NULL),
  (73499, 192, 'It''s reps of action that drive confidence.', 46.126, 49.629, NULL),
  (73500, 192, 'And that action, and that confidence
is what allows us to learn and grow.', 49.671, 53.383, NULL),
  (73501, 192, 'I''m someone who wants to continue
to learn and grow.', 53.425, 56.386, NULL),
  (73502, 192, 'No matter how old I get,', 56.428, 58.096, NULL),
  (73503, 192, 'how many successes or challenges,
how long I''ve been in a role or company,', 58.138, 62.350, NULL),
  (73504, 192, 'I want to get better.', 62.392, 64.060, NULL),
  (73505, 192, 'And you’re here, so I know you do, too.', 64.102, 66.479, NULL),
  (73506, 192, 'So the question is,
what techniques or practices', 66.479, 68.773, NULL),
  (73507, 192, 'can help us cut through the challenges
that are in our way to acting our way', 68.773, 73.778, NULL),
  (73508, 192, 'to confidence and growth.', 73.778, 75.363, NULL),
  (73509, 192, 'Many people believe
some of the best actions are', 75.363, 77.699, NULL),
  (73510, 192, 'when we show up in tough times,
and that''s true.', 77.699, 79.993, NULL),
  (73511, 192, 'But it''s almost easier
to take bold action when things are hard.', 79.993, 83.038, NULL),
  (73512, 192, 'There aren''t a lot of options.', 83.038, 84.789, NULL),
  (73513, 192, 'The more special muscle is the ability
to coach ourselves to be greater,', 84.831, 89.085, NULL),
  (73514, 192, 'to do more, to be better,
even when times are pretty good,', 89.127, 92.505, NULL),
  (73515, 192, 'and to recognize that complacency
is a very real thing,', 92.547, 96.801, NULL),
  (73516, 192, 'and we are all blinded
by our own progress.', 96.843, 99.888, NULL),
  (73517, 192, 'So one of the tools in my toolbox
to drive action and confidence and growth', 99.929, 104.184, NULL),
  (73518, 192, 'is the ability to cut through
that complacency.', 104.225, 107.395, NULL),
  (73519, 192, 'And I first learned
this lesson from my mom.', 107.437, 111.107, NULL),
  (73520, 192, 'When I was nine years old,', 111.107, 112.400, NULL),
  (73521, 192, 'my mom came to me and said,
"That''s it, I''m done. We''re leaving."', 112.400, 115.487, NULL),
  (73522, 192, 'And what she meant was
we were leaving my father.', 115.487, 117.906, NULL),
  (73523, 192, 'My father was and is a very good man.', 117.906, 121.618, NULL),
  (73524, 192, 'But at the time, he was an alcoholic
and a terrible husband and father.', 121.618, 125.664, NULL),
  (73525, 192, 'So when my mom came to me
at the age of nine,', 125.664, 128.416, NULL),
  (73526, 192, 'I didn’t cry, and I didn’t get upset.', 128.458, 131.628, NULL),
  (73527, 192, 'I remember thinking,
"What took you so long?', 131.670, 134.881, NULL),
  (73528, 192, 'Finally, it''s about time."', 134.923, 138.051, NULL),
  (73529, 192, 'So often there are people around us
just waiting on us to take the action,', 138.093, 142.514, NULL),
  (73530, 192, 'to do the thing, to do the right thing.', 142.555, 145.225, NULL),
  (73531, 192, 'And since then, I''ve been inspired', 145.266, 147.686, NULL),
  (73532, 192, 'to have practices
that drive action over and over.', 147.727, 150.730, NULL),
  (73533, 192, 'Little ones every day, or bigger ones,
like what my mom did that day.', 150.730, 155.485, NULL),
  (73534, 192, 'We did leave my dad.', 155.485, 156.778, NULL),
  (73535, 192, 'My mom fed us on a meager food budget,
worked multiple jobs for many years,', 156.778, 161.408, NULL),
  (73536, 192, 'and over the course of my young life,
I got to see her day-to-day example.', 161.408, 165.120, NULL),
  (73537, 192, 'Someone without resources,
without a playbook.', 165.120, 167.664, NULL),
  (73538, 192, 'She had no coach. She had no one
to mentor her through this experience.', 167.706, 172.419, NULL),
  (73539, 192, 'She just acted her way
to growth and improvement over time.', 172.460, 176.798, NULL),
  (73540, 192, 'As a result of this childhood,
I started working at a very young age.', 176.840, 180.093, NULL),
  (73541, 192, 'At 15, I worked in malls.', 180.135, 181.511, NULL),
  (73542, 192, 'At 17, I was a restaurant hostess,
at 18, a waitress.', 181.553, 184.556, NULL),
  (73543, 192, 'At 19, I began my leadership journey,
opening franchises around the world.', 184.597, 189.102, NULL),
  (73544, 192, 'By the age of 26, I was an executive
in a very large company.', 189.144, 194.023, NULL),
  (73545, 192, 'And while I had fantastic
supervisors and managers', 194.023, 198.862, NULL),
  (73546, 192, 'who helped me through my career,', 198.862, 200.989, NULL),
  (73547, 192, 'I lacked some of that
outside-in perspective.', 200.989, 203.450, NULL),
  (73548, 192, 'The mentoring, the things that could help
stretch me beyond my day-to-day job.', 203.450, 207.996, NULL),
  (73549, 192, 'So I started developing
some self-coaching practices.', 207.996, 211.624, NULL),
  (73550, 192, 'And one day I heard
from a restaurant consultant', 211.666, 215.003, NULL),
  (73551, 192, 'that you should sometimes imagine
someone else in your role', 215.044, 218.047, NULL),
  (73552, 192, 'to help motivate you to take action.', 218.089, 220.258, NULL),
  (73553, 192, 'So I started doing that, and it helped.', 220.300, 222.302, NULL),
  (73554, 192, 'So I started thinking
about people I admired,', 222.343, 225.346, NULL),
  (73555, 192, 'someone specific,', 225.388, 227.056, NULL),
  (73556, 192, 'and there was something
about thinking of someone I admired', 227.098, 229.934, NULL),
  (73557, 192, 'that brought this element
of additional capabilities and excellence.', 229.976, 233.480, NULL),
  (73558, 192, 'It also made me feel a little accountable
to act on whatever came to mind.', 233.480, 238.401, NULL),
  (73559, 192, 'And these practices evolved
into today what is the “hot shot rule.”', 238.401, 243.198, NULL),
  (73560, 192, 'The hot shot rule is simply this.', 243.198, 245.658, NULL),
  (73561, 192, 'It is the act of regularly thinking
about my role, everything I have,', 245.658, 251.539, NULL),
  (73562, 192, 'the challenges, the opportunities,', 251.581, 253.792, NULL),
  (73563, 192, 'envisioning someone I admire in my role,', 253.833, 256.795, NULL),
  (73564, 192, 'asking myself what''s one thing
that person I admire would do differently', 256.836, 260.381, NULL),
  (73565, 192, 'to make that situation better,', 260.423, 262.675, NULL),
  (73566, 192, 'acting on it within 24 hours,', 262.717, 264.886, NULL),
  (73567, 192, 'and then -- that''s not the last step --
telling those involved', 264.928, 268.431, NULL),
  (73568, 192, 'once things get put in motion.', 268.473, 270.016, NULL),
  (73569, 192, 'I say something like,', 270.058, 271.351, NULL),
  (73570, 192, '"Hey, I could have or should have
done this thing, but I didn''t.', 271.392, 274.395, NULL),
  (73571, 192, 'And now we are..."', 274.395, 275.647, NULL),
  (73572, 192, 'And so let''s practice it.', 275.647, 277.607, NULL),
  (73573, 192, 'So I think first of my role as a mother.', 277.607, 282.737, NULL),
  (73574, 192, 'I think of how I can be a better mom.', 282.737, 284.614, NULL),
  (73575, 192, 'I think of my role as daughter.', 284.614, 286.324, NULL),
  (73576, 192, 'I think of how I can be a better daughter,
and I envision someone I admire.', 286.324, 289.911, NULL),
  (73577, 192, 'But often, and we''re here
to talk about work,', 289.911, 292.038, NULL),
  (73578, 192, 'I think about my professional role.', 292.080, 293.790, NULL),
  (73579, 192, 'So I think about my role as CEO of AG1.', 293.832, 297.001, NULL),
  (73580, 192, 'I have this incredible opportunity
to be the leader', 297.043, 299.796, NULL),
  (73581, 192, 'of a phenomenal, foundational
nutrition company', 299.838, 302.382, NULL),
  (73582, 192, 'with millions of customers who rely on us
to empower their health journeys,', 302.423, 306.344, NULL),
  (73583, 192, 'and so many team members
who rely on me to be my best.', 306.386, 310.348, NULL),
  (73584, 192, 'Our customers and my team
deserve for me to be the best over time.', 310.390, 313.518, NULL),
  (73585, 192, 'Not comfortable because
we''ve had multiple years of success,', 313.560, 316.855, NULL),
  (73586, 192, 'but always starting
with that day one energy.', 316.855, 319.440, NULL),
  (73587, 192, 'Then I envision someone I admire.', 319.440, 321.442, NULL),
  (73588, 192, 'So I just met all of you,', 321.442, 323.152, NULL),
  (73589, 192, 'I think of you.', 323.152, 324.863, NULL),
  (73590, 192, 'Now I envision you in my seat tomorrow.', 324.863, 327.448, NULL),
  (73591, 192, 'I’m gone, and I’m just
watching you in my role.', 327.448, 330.076, NULL),
  (73592, 192, 'And I ask, what''s one thing
and the first thing', 330.076, 332.328, NULL),
  (73593, 192, 'you would do differently
to make the business better?', 332.328, 334.831, NULL),
  (73594, 192, 'And something comes to mind,
something actionable.', 334.873, 337.375, NULL),
  (73595, 192, 'I take action on it within 24 hours,', 337.417, 339.752, NULL),
  (73596, 192, 'and then once it''s in motion,
I tell my team.', 339.794, 342.422, NULL),
  (73597, 192, 'Practicing the hot shot rule over time', 342.463, 344.716, NULL),
  (73598, 192, 'has led to things like
flying to meet a business partner', 344.757, 347.635, NULL),
  (73599, 192, 'to hold them accountable
when I had made excuses for them.', 347.677, 350.388, NULL),
  (73600, 192, 'Or calling someone to apologize
or acknowledge a situation', 350.430, 353.850, NULL),
  (73601, 192, 'I could have handled
better or differently.', 353.892, 356.102, NULL),
  (73602, 192, 'It''s led to me thinking about someone', 356.144, 358.187, NULL),
  (73603, 192, 'who has recently lost
a parent or a loved one', 358.187, 362.108, NULL),
  (73604, 192, 'and envisioning them in my role.', 362.108, 364.027, NULL),
  (73605, 192, 'And it’s led to me
just picking up the phone', 364.027, 366.154, NULL),
  (73606, 192, 'and calling my mom, and saying,
“I love you, and how are you?”', 366.154, 369.407, NULL),
  (73607, 192, 'It''s led to me saying "thank you"
to my husband for being a great partner.', 369.407, 372.952, NULL),
  (73608, 192, 'It''s also led to me
stopping initiatives in the company', 372.952, 375.622, NULL),
  (73609, 192, 'that I was allowing to perpetuate', 375.622, 377.832, NULL),
  (73610, 192, 'because things were just comfortable,', 377.874, 379.667, NULL),
  (73611, 192, 'but they were no longer
serving the business.', 379.709, 382.462, NULL),
  (73612, 192, 'So that’s what the hot shot rule is.', 382.503, 384.380, NULL),
  (73613, 192, 'And you can use it as a technique
in a time of need anytime.', 384.422, 387.884, NULL),
  (73614, 192, 'But its power lies in it being
a regular, proactive practice.', 387.926, 392.180, NULL),
  (73615, 192, 'It used to be quarterly and then monthly,
but now I practice it weekly.', 392.221, 395.725, NULL),
  (73616, 192, 'Every Sunday at 1pm,', 395.767, 397.810, NULL),
  (73617, 192, 'when my kids, now five and seven,
used to have naps --', 397.852, 400.563, NULL),
  (73618, 192, 'RIP naps --', 400.563, 402.065, NULL),
  (73619, 192, '(Laughter)', 402.065, 403.358, NULL),
  (73620, 192, 'I take just a minute for myself.', 403.358, 405.777, NULL),
  (73621, 192, 'I envision my role,
I envision someone I admire.', 405.777, 408.821, NULL),
  (73622, 192, 'I ask myself, what''s one thing
they would do differently in my role.', 408.821, 412.075, NULL),
  (73623, 192, 'The answer comes to mind.', 412.075, 413.409, NULL),
  (73624, 192, 'I send the email, I schedule the flight,', 413.409, 415.370, NULL),
  (73625, 192, 'I put it in motion,', 415.370, 416.663, NULL),
  (73626, 192, 'and then once it''s in motion,
I tell my team.', 416.663, 418.790, NULL),
  (73627, 192, 'And over a year of practicing this weekly,
a few things will happen.', 418.831, 422.043, NULL),
  (73628, 192, 'One, there are 52 things you''ve done
that you otherwise might not have done', 422.085, 425.630, NULL),
  (73629, 192, 'or done as quickly.', 425.672, 426.965, NULL),
  (73630, 192, 'It builds a reputation
of vulnerability and bias for action.', 427.006, 429.842, NULL),
  (73631, 192, 'My team brings things to me now', 429.884, 431.511, NULL),
  (73632, 192, 'because they know
I''m constantly calling myself out.', 431.552, 434.764, NULL),
  (73633, 192, 'This practice has changed my life,', 434.806, 436.432, NULL),
  (73634, 192, 'and I believe it will change yours
if you apply it.', 436.474, 440.103, NULL),
  (73635, 192, 'The idea of having a practice
of reflection, intention and action', 440.144, 444.732, NULL),
  (73636, 192, 'to drive growth,
to show up and do something', 444.732, 447.068, NULL),
  (73637, 192, 'we otherwise wouldn’t have,', 447.068, 448.611, NULL),
  (73638, 192, 'to break through complacency
or past patterns is a superpower.', 448.611, 453.366, NULL),
  (73639, 192, 'So be like my mom.', 453.366, 455.201, NULL),
  (73640, 192, 'Don''t let patterns of the past
get in the way', 455.201, 457.370, NULL),
  (73641, 192, 'of doing something different tomorrow.', 457.370, 459.205, NULL),
  (73642, 192, 'Ask questions that help motivate action.', 459.247, 462.000, NULL),
  (73643, 192, 'And act your way
into growth and confidence.', 462.041, 465.211, NULL),
  (73644, 192, 'Thank you.', 465.253, 466.504, NULL),
  (73645, 192, '(Applause)', 466.546, 468.548, NULL),
  (73646, 193, 'So I vividly remember
my first anxiety attack.', 4.101, 7.638, NULL),
  (73647, 193, 'It''s kind of like I feel right now.', 9.073, 10.775, NULL),
  (73648, 193, '(Laughter)', 10.808, 12.143, NULL),
  (73649, 193, 'Whoo, is it hot in here?', 12.143, 13.744, NULL),
  (73650, 193, '(Laughter)', 13.744, 15.446, NULL),
  (73651, 193, 'It''s hot in here.', 15.479, 16.680, NULL),
  (73652, 193, '(Laughter)', 16.680, 17.748, NULL),
  (73653, 193, 'This wave of fear crashed over me,
and my heart started to pound.', 17.748, 24.121, NULL),
  (73654, 193, 'My breathing got ahead of me
and out of control.', 24.155, 27.324, NULL),
  (73655, 193, 'My face felt hot.', 27.324, 29.193, NULL),
  (73656, 193, 'It''s hot in here, right?', 29.193, 30.394, NULL),
  (73657, 193, '(Laughter)', 30.394, 31.395, NULL),
  (73658, 193, 'Yeah, it''s hot.', 31.429, 32.596, NULL),
  (73659, 193, 'And I got doused in this really
uncomfortable cold sweat.', 32.630, 36.367, NULL),
  (73660, 193, 'It was a life-changing moment,', 38.636, 40.304, NULL),
  (73661, 193, 'because I made a decision,
right there and then,', 40.337, 44.742, NULL),
  (73662, 193, 'to dedicate my career to ridding our world
of this feeling, anxiety.', 44.775, 50.681, NULL),
  (73663, 193, 'So that was more than two decades ago.', 52.583, 55.319, NULL),
  (73664, 193, 'Work in progress.', 57.154, 58.322, NULL),
  (73665, 193, '(Laughter)', 58.355, 61.025, NULL),
  (73666, 193, 'I became a clinical psychologist.', 61.058, 62.760, NULL),
  (73667, 193, 'I became a professor.', 62.793, 64.929, NULL),
  (73668, 193, 'I started an anxiety treatment center.', 64.962, 67.498, NULL),
  (73669, 193, 'And then, I realized,
at some point along the way,', 68.399, 70.901, NULL),
  (73670, 193, 'that eradicating anxiety
from our lives would not be beneficial.', 70.901, 75.806, NULL),
  (73671, 193, 'Sometimes, anxiety interferes
with your life.', 80.478, 83.414, NULL),
  (73672, 193, 'That''s clinical anxiety.', 83.447, 85.483, NULL),
  (73673, 193, 'And yes, you do want
to get rid of that clinical anxiety,', 85.516, 88.853, NULL),
  (73674, 193, 'with the help of a professional.', 88.886, 90.988, NULL),
  (73675, 193, 'But other times, many times ...', 91.021, 93.557, NULL),
  (73676, 193, 'it''s uncomfortable, it''s uncontrollable.', 95.159, 98.295, NULL),
  (73677, 193, 'Did I mention it''s hot in here?', 98.329, 99.897, NULL),
  (73678, 193, '(Laughter)', 99.897, 101.365, NULL),
  (73679, 193, 'It''s intense.', 102.166, 103.334, NULL),
  (73680, 193, 'But that''s a good thing.', 103.367, 104.869, NULL),
  (73681, 193, 'It''s a good thing.', 104.902, 106.337, NULL),
  (73682, 193, 'Many of the greatest leaders
in human history,', 110.908, 115.312, NULL),
  (73683, 193, 'certainly in recent history,', 115.346, 117.915, NULL),
  (73684, 193, 'they were forged in a cauldron of anxiety.', 117.948, 122.086, NULL),
  (73685, 193, 'Once, early in his career,
Sir Winston Churchill,', 123.854, 126.790, NULL),
  (73686, 193, 'he froze for three full minutes
in the House of Commons,', 126.790, 130.594, NULL),
  (73687, 193, 'giving a speech.', 130.628, 131.896, NULL),
  (73688, 193, 'He fought against his phobia,', 134.365, 136.500, NULL),
  (73689, 193, 'faced his fears head-on,', 136.534, 137.902, NULL),
  (73690, 193, 'and he went on to become
one of the greatest orators', 137.935, 141.438, NULL),
  (73691, 193, 'of the 20th century.', 141.472, 143.073, NULL),
  (73692, 193, 'In the 1990s,', 144.642, 146.143, NULL),
  (73693, 193, 'after a box-office flop, Oprah Winfrey,', 146.177, 150.447, NULL),
  (73694, 193, 'she turned to food
to drown out her feelings,', 150.481, 153.884, NULL),
  (73695, 193, 'to suppress her emotions.', 153.918, 155.386, NULL),
  (73696, 193, 'She ended up feeling
emotionally numb for six weeks,', 155.419, 159.056, NULL),
  (73697, 193, 'and during that period of great anxiety,', 159.089, 161.392, NULL),
  (73698, 193, 'she learned the importance of letting go
of her expectations for success.', 161.425, 167.731, NULL),
  (73699, 193, 'She went on to become a media icon.', 167.765, 169.667, NULL),
  (73700, 193, 'And speaking of icons ...', 170.634, 172.236, NULL),
  (73701, 193, 'The first time Taylor Swift sang
the national anthem at a football game,', 173.904, 179.410, NULL),
  (73702, 193, 'she felt paralyzed with fear.', 179.443, 181.645, NULL),
  (73703, 193, 'What she learned is to share
her feelings with others.', 183.914, 186.584, NULL),
  (73704, 193, 'Listen to her lyrics.', 187.418, 188.552, NULL),
  (73705, 193, 'Many of them speak about her own anxiety.', 188.586, 190.788, NULL),
  (73706, 193, 'And now, well, apparently,
she can “shake it off.”', 190.821, 193.591, NULL),
  (73707, 193, '(Laughter)', 193.624, 197.628, NULL),
  (73708, 193, 'Anxiety is an emotion,', 197.661, 200.197, NULL),
  (73709, 193, 'like any other emotion,', 200.231, 202.132, NULL),
  (73710, 193, 'and it can do so much good for you.', 202.166, 205.135, NULL),
  (73711, 193, 'It can increase your resilience.', 205.169, 207.304, NULL),
  (73712, 193, 'It can strengthen your relationships.', 207.338, 209.440, NULL),
  (73713, 193, 'And it can help you to let go.', 210.241, 212.443, NULL),
  (73714, 193, 'When I first met Nicole ...', 212.443, 214.245, NULL),
  (73715, 193, 'she had hypochondriasis,
which is clinical health anxiety.', 215.446, 218.582, NULL),
  (73716, 193, 'Despite numerous MRIs to the contrary,', 219.416, 221.885, NULL),
  (73717, 193, 'she was convinced
that she had an aneurysm.', 221.919, 224.855, NULL),
  (73718, 193, 'Nicole''s biggest fear
was that her anxiety would spike,', 226.023, 230.060, NULL),
  (73719, 193, 'her brain would explode,', 230.094, 233.364, NULL),
  (73720, 193, 'and she would drop dead,', 233.397, 234.632, NULL),
  (73721, 193, 'which would not be good.', 234.665, 236.467, NULL),
  (73722, 193, 'Nicole started to withdraw
from daily activities,', 236.467, 239.103, NULL),
  (73723, 193, 'and she recognized, rightfully,
that she needed professional help,', 239.136, 242.973, NULL),
  (73724, 193, 'so she came in.', 243.007, 244.308, NULL),
  (73725, 193, 'Nicole overcame her obsessions
with exposure therapy.', 245.476, 250.114, NULL),
  (73726, 193, 'She faced her fears.', 250.914, 252.316, NULL),
  (73727, 193, 'She embraced them head-on
in order to build resilience.', 252.349, 256.053, NULL),
  (73728, 193, 'She read stories about aneurysms.', 257.087, 258.689, NULL),
  (73729, 193, 'She watched videos about aneurysms.', 258.722, 260.524, NULL),
  (73730, 193, 'She went to a local neurology ward.', 260.557, 263.093, NULL),
  (73731, 193, 'Nicole overcame her obsessions,', 263.127, 267.197, NULL),
  (73732, 193, 'and she graduated from therapy.', 267.197, 268.766, NULL),
  (73733, 193, 'I was so happy and so proud of her.', 268.766, 271.669, NULL),
  (73734, 193, 'And then, a couple years later,
the phone rang.', 272.436, 277.007, NULL),
  (73735, 193, 'Nicole tells me she''s pregnant
with a baby boy,', 277.007, 280.944, NULL),
  (73736, 193, 'but the doctors told her
that he would probably die', 280.978, 285.382, NULL),
  (73737, 193, 'because an ultrasound revealed
that he had an aneurysm.', 285.416, 288.886, NULL),
  (73738, 193, 'Now given Nicole''s history,
I thought she would fall apart.', 288.919, 293.023, NULL),
  (73739, 193, 'But she didn''t. She didn''t.', 293.057, 296.126, NULL),
  (73740, 193, 'The baby needed life-saving surgery
shortly after birth,', 296.160, 299.263, NULL),
  (73741, 193, 'and Nicole, understandably
and very appropriately,', 299.296, 302.599, NULL),
  (73742, 193, 'was very anxious during the surgery,
as the doctors operated.', 302.633, 307.137, NULL),
  (73743, 193, 'But she stuck with it,', 307.137, 309.039, NULL),
  (73744, 193, 'and so did he.', 309.073, 310.474, NULL),
  (73745, 193, 'Today, he is a healthy,
thriving little boy,', 311.175, 313.744, NULL),
  (73746, 193, 'and also really cute, by the way.', 313.777, 315.579, NULL),
  (73747, 193, 'Really cute. Cute kid.', 315.612, 317.481, NULL),
  (73748, 193, 'And Nicole, she is a super-resilient mom
because she faced anxiety.', 317.514, 322.786, NULL),
  (73749, 193, 'You are a lot more like Nicole
than you think.', 325.556, 328.225, NULL),
  (73750, 193, 'There have been many times in your life
where you, too, embraced anxiety.', 329.693, 333.297, NULL),
  (73751, 193, 'When you embraced the discomfort,', 333.330, 335.032, NULL),
  (73752, 193, 'when you persevered,
although you felt panicky and worried.', 335.065, 339.370, NULL),
  (73753, 193, 'And you''ve done this because,
deep in your heart,', 341.271, 343.574, NULL),
  (73754, 193, 'you know that you cannot
get rid of all of your anxiety,', 343.607, 346.477, NULL),
  (73755, 193, 'and it will always be uncomfortable.', 346.477, 348.312, NULL),
  (73756, 193, 'And that''s why pushing against it
creates mental muscle tone,', 348.345, 352.916, NULL),
  (73757, 193, 'which you need ...', 352.950, 354.151, NULL),
  (73758, 193, 'to crest over life''s hurdles with grace.', 355.652, 358.722, NULL),
  (73759, 193, 'It can be difficult to love someone
who has anxiety,', 359.890, 364.328, NULL),
  (73760, 193, 'and it''s probably even more
difficult to receive it.', 364.361, 368.132, NULL),
  (73761, 193, 'But deep human connection,', 369.032, 372.403, NULL),
  (73762, 193, 'deep emotional connections between people,', 372.436, 375.072, NULL),
  (73763, 193, 'requires vulnerability.', 375.105, 377.474, NULL),
  (73764, 193, 'So anxiety can be used to create intimacy.', 378.075, 382.079, NULL),
  (73765, 193, 'Think about it.', 384.014, 385.149, NULL),
  (73766, 193, 'In your own life, who are the people
who you feel closest to?', 385.182, 388.652, NULL),
  (73767, 193, 'Usually, it''s those
who you''ve opened up to', 390.187, 392.623, NULL),
  (73768, 193, 'about your anxiety in some way.', 392.656, 394.691, NULL),
  (73769, 193, 'I myself --', 395.926, 397.661, NULL),
  (73770, 193, 'This is going to be hard, but I''ll try.', 397.694, 399.630, NULL),
  (73771, 193, 'I''m terrified of failure.', 402.566, 404.268, NULL),
  (73772, 193, 'I''m terrified of professional failure.', 404.968, 406.970, NULL),
  (73773, 193, 'And I struggle with vulnerability.', 407.805, 410.040, NULL),
  (73774, 193, 'In some ways, this propelled me', 410.841, 412.910, NULL),
  (73775, 193, 'and fueled my drive
for professional success.', 412.943, 416.880, NULL),
  (73776, 193, 'But it created distance
in my relationships.', 416.914, 420.651, NULL),
  (73777, 193, 'When I first met my wonderful,
wonderful wife, Miri ...', 420.684, 423.787, NULL),
  (73778, 193, 'I put up a wall,', 425.355, 426.557, NULL),
  (73779, 193, 'and I didn''t speak enough
about my feelings,', 426.590, 428.926, NULL),
  (73780, 193, 'and I submerged my anxiety
by focusing on my work.', 428.959, 431.662, NULL),
  (73781, 193, 'Right? Pretty classic, right?', 431.695, 433.664, NULL),
  (73782, 193, '(Laughter)', 433.697, 434.698, NULL),
  (73783, 193, 'You don''t need to be a psychotherapist
to figure that one out.', 434.731, 437.701, NULL),
  (73784, 193, '(Laughter)', 437.734, 438.869, NULL),
  (73785, 193, 'Of course, the feelings didn''t go away.', 440.137, 442.773, NULL),
  (73786, 193, 'We all have this, like, chef,
in the back of our emotional kitchen.', 442.806, 448.045, NULL),
  (73787, 193, 'Well, my chef cooked up
these entrées of edginess,', 448.078, 452.182, NULL),
  (73788, 193, 'side orders of criticism', 452.216, 454.785, NULL),
  (73789, 193, 'and a whole bunch of other dishes', 454.818, 456.520, NULL),
  (73790, 193, 'that I''m not going
to speak about in public.', 456.520, 458.755, NULL),
  (73791, 193, '(Laughter)', 458.755, 461.058, NULL),
  (73792, 193, 'But Miri, thankfully, stuck with me.', 461.391, 464.127, NULL),
  (73793, 193, 'And more importantly,', 464.661, 465.896, NULL),
  (73794, 193, 'she consistently showed me
that she would never judge me if I failed.', 465.929, 469.733, NULL),
  (73795, 193, 'Eventually, I got the message.', 472.803, 474.438, NULL),
  (73796, 193, 'It took a while,', 474.471, 476.306, NULL),
  (73797, 193, 'but that unconditional love
that I received', 476.306, 479.476, NULL),
  (73798, 193, 'allowed me to take the plunge,', 479.510, 482.312, NULL),
  (73799, 193, 'drop my guard, lower my defenses', 482.312, 485.883, NULL),
  (73800, 193, 'and identify what I was afraid of
and to share it with her.', 485.916, 489.486, NULL),
  (73801, 193, 'I think it''s the hardest thing
I ever did my whole life.', 491.488, 494.291, NULL),
  (73802, 193, 'Definitely harder than anything
in the professional realm.', 494.324, 497.828, NULL),
  (73803, 193, 'But there''s nothing more worthwhile', 499.630, 501.665, NULL),
  (73804, 193, 'than taking our anxiety
and turning it into love.', 501.698, 504.868, NULL),
  (73805, 193, 'Losing control is utterly terrifying.', 506.603, 512.175, NULL),
  (73806, 193, 'It''s terrifying.', 513.310, 514.745, NULL),
  (73807, 193, 'It''s happened to everyone.', 514.778, 516.713, NULL),
  (73808, 193, 'But, but ...', 517.814, 520.484, NULL),
  (73809, 193, 'As long as you have a heads-up,', 522.085, 524.621, NULL),
  (73810, 193, 'as long as you expect it
and you''re a willing participant,', 524.621, 528.792, NULL),
  (73811, 193, 'doesn''t it feel good to let go?', 528.825, 531.228, NULL),
  (73812, 193, 'You don''t need to be a thrill-seeker
to appreciate this.', 534.464, 538.302, NULL),
  (73813, 193, 'Adrenaline ...', 538.335, 539.736, NULL),
  (73814, 193, 'A shot of it comes with pure joy', 540.737, 543.073, NULL),
  (73815, 193, 'followed by this blissful tranquility,', 543.106, 545.409, NULL),
  (73816, 193, 'like, wow.', 545.442, 547.210, NULL),
  (73817, 193, 'And perhaps for that reason,', 551.181, 552.549, NULL),
  (73818, 193, 'even in this age of unprecedented,
incredible anxiety,', 552.583, 558.288, NULL),
  (73819, 193, 'action and adventure movies,', 558.322, 559.990, NULL),
  (73820, 193, 'they make up more than 50 percent
of box-office sales.', 560.023, 563.160, NULL),
  (73821, 193, 'And the most profitable genre
of film is horror.', 563.160, 566.496, NULL),
  (73822, 193, '(Laughter)', 566.530, 567.698, NULL),
  (73823, 193, 'It''s funny.', 567.731, 568.999, NULL),
  (73824, 193, '(Laughter)', 569.032, 570.467, NULL),
  (73825, 193, 'Now life isn''t a movie,', 571.301, 574.137, NULL),
  (73826, 193, 'so it''s very good to shape the world
in accordance with your vision', 574.171, 578.942, NULL),
  (73827, 193, 'on a daily basis.', 578.976, 580.177, NULL),
  (73828, 193, 'It''s very important that we do that.', 580.210, 582.646, NULL),
  (73829, 193, 'But, once in a while ...', 582.679, 584.781, NULL),
  (73830, 193, 'It''s a human need to take a seat', 585.949, 589.286, NULL),
  (73831, 193, 'and go for a ride
on the roller coaster of life,', 589.319, 592.689, NULL),
  (73832, 193, 'to let go.', 592.723, 593.857, NULL),
  (73833, 193, '(Laughter)', 593.890, 596.827, NULL),
  (73834, 193, 'Doing so keeps your ego in check.', 598.195, 600.397, NULL),
  (73835, 193, 'Some people view this surrender
in spiritual terms.', 603.200, 607.771, NULL),
  (73836, 193, 'The Serenity Prayer,', 609.006, 610.574, NULL),
  (73837, 193, 'very commonly used to cope with anxiety,', 610.607, 614.978, NULL),
  (73838, 193, 'and it famously states', 615.012, 616.580, NULL),
  (73839, 193, '"God, grant me the serenity
to accept the things I cannot change."', 616.613, 621.151, NULL),
  (73840, 193, 'Now when you''re ready --', 622.753, 624.054, NULL),
  (73841, 193, 'not before you''re ready, please,
but when you''re ready --', 624.087, 627.090, NULL),
  (73842, 193, 'affirming the limits of your control ...', 627.124, 630.894, NULL),
  (73843, 193, 'it brings inner peace.', 631.762, 633.196, NULL),
  (73844, 193, 'Anxiety is nothing to be ashamed of.', 634.931, 637.334, NULL),
  (73845, 193, 'We all have it.', 638.502, 640.037, NULL),
  (73846, 193, 'And it''s not going away.', 641.805, 643.473, NULL),
  (73847, 193, 'Here are four steps that you can use', 646.710, 651.615, NULL),
  (73848, 193, 'to turn anxiety into your ally,
not your enemy.', 651.615, 654.117, NULL),
  (73849, 193, 'But please, if anxiety interferes
with your life, if it''s clinical,', 654.151, 659.256, NULL),
  (73850, 193, 'don''t just rely on this approach.', 659.289, 661.091, NULL),
  (73851, 193, 'Get the professional help you need.', 661.124, 663.026, NULL),
  (73852, 193, 'If we have an agreement on that,
then I''ll tell you the four steps.', 663.026, 666.329, NULL),
  (73853, 193, '(Laughter)', 666.363, 668.832, NULL),
  (73854, 193, 'OK. Step number one -- identify.', 668.865, 671.668, NULL),
  (73855, 193, 'Many times, when you feel anxious,
you squelch the sensations', 673.070, 676.073, NULL),
  (73856, 193, 'and push them out of your mind', 676.106, 677.607, NULL),
  (73857, 193, 'before you''ve even processed
what you''re worried about.', 677.641, 680.477, NULL),
  (73858, 193, 'Stop.', 680.510, 682.546, NULL),
  (73859, 193, 'Take a minute and ask yourself,
"What am I truly afraid of?"', 682.579, 688.618, NULL),
  (73860, 193, 'Like what really is
at the bottom of my fear?', 688.652, 691.088, NULL),
  (73861, 193, 'If you don''t know the answer, that''s fine.', 692.255, 694.324, NULL),
  (73862, 193, 'Go for a walk and don''t come back
until you have an answer.', 694.357, 697.160, NULL),
  (73863, 193, '(Laughter)', 697.160, 698.795, NULL),
  (73864, 193, 'Step two -- share.', 700.530, 702.332, NULL),
  (73865, 193, 'Speak about your anxiety,', 703.867, 706.336, NULL),
  (73866, 193, 'with a friend, with a neighbor,
with a coworker,', 706.336, 709.306, NULL),
  (73867, 193, 'with a stranger.', 709.339, 710.974, NULL),
  (73868, 193, 'I''m serious.', 712.342, 714.144, NULL),
  (73869, 193, 'If you''re not ready
for a conversation, that''s fine.', 715.946, 718.381, NULL),
  (73870, 193, 'Text it.', 718.415, 719.883, NULL),
  (73871, 193, 'If it''s more than a couple lines, sure.', 719.916, 721.885, NULL),
  (73872, 193, 'Email. Press send.', 721.918, 724.321, NULL),
  (73873, 193, 'Take the plunge. Be vulnerable.', 725.922, 729.392, NULL),
  (73874, 193, 'Step three -- embrace.', 730.861, 733.296, NULL),
  (73875, 193, 'When you feel anxious --', 733.997, 735.398, NULL),
  (73876, 193, 'not "if" -- you will.', 735.398, 738.368, NULL),
  (73877, 193, 'You will feel anxious.', 738.401, 739.569, NULL),
  (73878, 193, 'And when it happens, don''t fight it.', 739.569, 742.806, NULL),
  (73879, 193, 'Don''t squelch it.', 743.740, 745.642, NULL),
  (73880, 193, 'Let it happen, let it ride, let it ride.', 745.675, 748.779, NULL),
  (73881, 193, 'In fact, do things
that make you uncomfortable.', 750.213, 753.116, NULL),
  (73882, 193, 'Intentionally. Repeatedly.', 753.150, 755.452, NULL),
  (73883, 193, 'As long as they''re safe.', 755.485, 758.288, NULL),
  (73884, 193, 'That''s how we build emotional resilience.', 758.288, 761.424, NULL),
  (73885, 193, 'And finally, my favorite, four.', 762.692, 764.327, NULL),
  (73886, 193, 'Let go.', 764.361, 766.229, NULL),
  (73887, 193, 'Let go.', 767.631, 769.266, NULL),
  (73888, 193, 'Think back to step number one.', 769.266, 772.002, NULL),
  (73889, 193, 'What are you truly afraid of?', 772.035, 773.436, NULL),
  (73890, 193, 'And then, when you''re ready, humbly admit,', 773.470, 777.174, NULL),
  (73891, 193, 'even for a moment,', 777.207, 778.608, NULL),
  (73892, 193, 'that you are not in full control
of that outcome.', 778.642, 780.944, NULL),
  (73893, 193, 'It''s scary to even think about,
but it''s not a bad thing.', 783.046, 786.216, NULL),
  (73894, 193, 'Firstly, sometimes challenges
are a blessing in disguise,', 786.249, 789.419, NULL),
  (73895, 193, 'but either way,', 789.452, 793.223, NULL),
  (73896, 193, 'enjoy not being responsible
for everything under the sun.', 793.256, 798.061, NULL),
  (73897, 193, 'OK, should I try the four steps?', 800.130, 803.099, NULL),
  (73898, 193, 'Yeah, I''ll give it a shot.', 803.133, 804.901, NULL),
  (73899, 193, 'Identify.', 805.602, 806.736, NULL),
  (73900, 193, 'The hardest part about this talk
was speaking about my anxiety in public.', 808.205, 812.776, NULL),
  (73901, 193, 'I was afraid you would judge me.', 814.277, 815.879, NULL),
  (73902, 193, 'It''s really quiet in here.', 818.215, 819.583, NULL),
  (73903, 193, 'Did you judge me?', 819.616, 820.784, NULL),
  (73904, 193, '(Laughter)', 820.817, 822.752, NULL),
  (73905, 193, 'OK. That made me really anxious.', 822.752, 824.454, NULL),
  (73906, 193, '(Laughter)', 824.487, 826.656, NULL),
  (73907, 193, 'Share.', 826.690, 827.858, NULL),
  (73908, 193, 'OK, so I''m revealing this to you now', 827.858, 829.693, NULL),
  (73909, 193, 'because we''ve spent,
like, 10 minutes together,', 829.726, 831.962, NULL),
  (73910, 193, 'and I''ve grown to like you.', 831.995, 833.496, NULL),
  (73911, 193, 'So I want more of an emotional
connection here,', 833.530, 836.032, NULL),
  (73912, 193, 'and I hope it''s mutual.', 836.032, 837.734, NULL),
  (73913, 193, '(Laughter)', 837.767, 838.768, NULL),
  (73914, 193, 'OK, thanks.', 838.768, 839.936, NULL),
  (73915, 193, '(Cheers and applause)', 839.970, 846.977, NULL),
  (73916, 193, '(Exhales)', 847.344, 848.478, NULL),
  (73917, 193, '(Laughter)', 848.511, 849.546, NULL),
  (73918, 193, 'Three -- embrace.', 849.579, 850.814, NULL),
  (73919, 193, 'Do you know what it''s like
to stand on this red dot', 850.847, 854.150, NULL),
  (73920, 193, 'and to speak about,
like, all your issues in public?', 854.150, 857.587, NULL),
  (73921, 193, '(Laughter)', 857.587, 858.889, NULL),
  (73922, 193, 'It''s like diving off a cliff.', 858.922, 860.323, NULL),
  (73923, 193, 'Especially, remember that part
about my emotional kitchen?', 860.323, 863.260, NULL),
  (73924, 193, 'Like, that was really vulnerable for me.', 863.293, 865.228, NULL),
  (73925, 193, '(Laughter)', 865.228, 867.397, NULL),
  (73926, 193, 'And let go.', 867.430, 868.565, NULL),
  (73927, 193, 'So I''m sending this message
about anxiety off into the universe.', 868.598, 872.802, NULL),
  (73928, 193, 'I hope that it will land on the hearts,
minds and souls of a broader audience.', 872.836, 877.073, NULL),
  (73929, 193, 'But really, there''s nothing
I can do about that anymore.', 877.107, 880.510, NULL),
  (73930, 193, '(Laughter)', 880.543, 881.544, NULL),
  (73931, 193, 'And that''s OK.', 881.578, 882.946, NULL),
  (73932, 193, 'That''s OK.', 883.313, 884.447, NULL),
  (73933, 193, 'So please join me.', 885.949, 887.217, NULL),
  (73934, 193, 'What are the four steps?', 887.250, 888.418, NULL),
  (73935, 193, 'Let''s say them together so we remember.', 888.451, 890.420, NULL),
  (73936, 193, '(With the audience)
Identify, share, embrace, let go.', 890.420, 894.991, NULL),
  (73937, 193, 'Thank you very much.', 894.991, 896.192, NULL),
  (73938, 193, '(Applause)', 896.226, 899.095, NULL),
  (73939, 194, 'So today, what I want to do', 4.334, 5.669, NULL),
  (73940, 194, 'is talk to you about the most important
conversations you have each day:', 5.710, 9.422, NULL),
  (73941, 194, 'the conversations
you have with yourselves.', 9.464, 11.716, NULL),
  (73942, 194, 'My name is Ethan Kross.', 11.716, 13.009, NULL),
  (73943, 194, 'I’m the director of the 
Emotion and Self Control Lab', 13.009, 15.512, NULL),
  (73944, 194, 'at the University of Michigan,', 15.512, 17.013, NULL),
  (73945, 194, 'and for the past 25 years,', 17.013, 18.348, NULL),
  (73946, 194, 'I''ve been studying how people
can manage their emotions.', 18.348, 21.726, NULL),
  (73947, 194, 'And one of the things that I''ve learned
during that time -- (Object drops)', 21.768, 25.438, NULL),
  (73948, 194, 'See? I''m managing my emotions right now.', 25.438, 27.357, NULL),
  (73949, 194, '(Laughter)', 27.399, 28.817, NULL),
  (73950, 194, 'One of the things
that I''ve learned during that time', 28.858, 32.153, NULL),
  (73951, 194, 'is that a key to managing
one''s emotions effectively', 32.195, 35.156, NULL),
  (73952, 194, 'involves understanding
how to harness this mysterious force', 35.198, 39.661, NULL),
  (73953, 194, 'called the voices inside our head.', 39.661, 42.581, NULL),
  (73954, 194, 'Now I realize some of you
may be asking yourself right now,', 42.581, 45.709, NULL),
  (73955, 194, '“What is a purported
serious scientist doing', 45.709, 48.378, NULL),
  (73956, 194, 'talking about a squishy topic
like the voices inside our head?"', 48.378, 53.550, NULL),
  (73957, 194, 'But I want to point out
the elephant in the room --', 53.550, 55.969, NULL),
  (73958, 194, 'that, you know, if you''ve just asked
yourself that question,', 55.969, 59.180, NULL),
  (73959, 194, 'you are talking to yourself.', 59.222, 61.433, NULL),
  (73960, 194, 'And that''s totally OK,', 61.433, 63.226, NULL),
  (73961, 194, 'because the vast majority of us
have a voice inside our head.', 63.226, 67.480, NULL),
  (73962, 194, 'Here''s a scientific fact
that I absolutely love.', 67.522, 70.150, NULL),
  (73963, 194, 'We spend between one half and 
one-third of our waking hours', 70.191, 73.445, NULL),
  (73964, 194, 'not focused on the present.', 73.486, 75.447, NULL),
  (73965, 194, 'Between one half
and one-third of the time,', 75.488, 77.532, NULL),
  (73966, 194, 'our minds, they are drifting away.', 77.574, 79.284, NULL),
  (73967, 194, 'We are thinking about other things.', 79.284, 81.328, NULL),
  (73968, 194, 'Some of you are doing that right now.', 81.369, 83.163, NULL),
  (73969, 194, 'Please stop.', 83.622, 84.789, NULL),
  (73970, 194, '(Laughter)', 84.831, 86.750, NULL),
  (73971, 194, 'Once we find ourselves drifting away,', 86.750, 89.169, NULL),
  (73972, 194, 'one of the things that we''re doing
is talking to ourselves', 89.210, 92.964, NULL),
  (73973, 194, 'and listening to what we say.', 92.964, 95.592, NULL),
  (73974, 194, 'Now when scientists like myself
use the term “inner voice,”', 95.592, 98.470, NULL),
  (73975, 194, 'what we''re talking about
is our ability to silently use language', 98.511, 101.556, NULL),
  (73976, 194, 'to reflect on our lives.', 101.598, 102.807, NULL),
  (73977, 194, 'And it turns out this is one
of your superpowers,', 102.849, 105.143, NULL),
  (73978, 194, 'because your inner voice lets you keep
information active in your head', 105.143, 108.772, NULL),
  (73979, 194, 'for short periods of time,', 108.813, 110.899, NULL),
  (73980, 194, 'like when you go to the grocery store.', 110.940, 112.817, NULL),
  (73981, 194, 'And if you''re like me,
15 seconds into the expedition,', 112.859, 116.071, NULL),
  (73982, 194, 'you forget what you’re supposed to buy,
and you repeat that list in your head.', 116.071, 120.283, NULL),
  (73983, 194, '"Apples, cheese. Pepto Bismol."', 120.283, 123.578, NULL),
  (73984, 194, 'TMI.', 124.829, 126.122, NULL),
  (73985, 194, 'We also use our inner voice
to simulate and plan,', 126.164, 129.668, NULL),
  (73986, 194, 'like when we silently rehearse
what we''re going to say', 129.709, 132.379, NULL),
  (73987, 194, 'before an important presentation
or an interview.', 132.379, 135.590, NULL),
  (73988, 194, 'And of course, we use our inner voice
to control and motivate ourselves,', 135.632, 140.470, NULL),
  (73989, 194, 'as I did just before I came on stage.', 140.470, 143.682, NULL),
  (73990, 194, 'It''s right around the corner, over there.', 143.723, 145.684, NULL),
  (73991, 194, 'I silently said to myself, "Come on, man,
you''ve got this. Deep breath.', 145.725, 150.313, NULL),
  (73992, 194, '45 minutes, and you are done.”', 150.313, 152.190, NULL),
  (73993, 194, '(Laughter)', 152.232, 153.483, NULL),
  (73994, 194, 'And of course, all of you
just said to yourself,', 153.525, 155.860, NULL),
  (73995, 194, '"This guy thinks he''s talking
for 45 minutes. He''s nuts."', 155.860, 158.780, NULL),
  (73996, 194, '(Laughter)', 158.780, 159.864, NULL),
  (73997, 194, 'Finally, perhaps most magically,', 159.864, 163.118, NULL),
  (73998, 194, 'we use our inner voice to make sense
of this messy world that we often live in.', 163.159, 169.499, NULL),
  (73999, 194, 'When we experience challenges,
we turn our attention inward,', 170.041, 173.002, NULL),
  (74000, 194, 'and we try to work through them.', 173.044, 175.213, NULL),
  (74001, 194, 'And our inner voice
helps us create those stories', 175.255, 178.007, NULL),
  (74002, 194, 'that shape our sense of self,', 178.049, 180.427, NULL),
  (74003, 194, 'stories that really craft our identity.', 180.427, 182.470, NULL),
  (74004, 194, 'So your inner voice,
this is a remarkable tool.', 182.512, 186.516, NULL),
  (74005, 194, 'The problem is it is a tool that often
jams up on us when we need it most.', 186.558, 192.147, NULL),
  (74006, 194, 'We don''t come up with clear
solutions to our problems.', 192.188, 196.025, NULL),
  (74007, 194, 'We get stuck in negative
thought loops, instead.', 196.067, 198.486, NULL),
  (74008, 194, 'We worry. We ruminate.', 198.528, 200.905, NULL),
  (74009, 194, 'We experience what I call the dark side
of our inner voice: chatter.', 200.905, 204.826, NULL),
  (74010, 194, 'How do you know
if you''re experiencing chatter?', 205.368, 207.787, NULL),
  (74011, 194, 'If you ever find yourself
trying to work through a problem', 207.829, 210.665, NULL),
  (74012, 194, 'but not making any progress,', 210.707, 212.375, NULL),
  (74013, 194, 'or if you find yourself
berating yourself incessantly --', 212.417, 216.171, NULL),
  (74014, 194, '"I''m an idiot, such an idiot."', 216.212, 218.465, NULL),
  (74015, 194, 'Those are two telltale signs.', 218.506, 220.425, NULL),
  (74016, 194, 'Now if this description of chatter
resonates with any of you here --', 221.217, 224.554, NULL),
  (74017, 194, 'I''m sure it does not.', 224.596, 226.139, NULL),
  (74018, 194, 'But if it does,', 226.139, 227.640, NULL),
  (74019, 194, 'my response to you is welcome
to the human condition, my friends.', 227.682, 232.771, NULL),
  (74020, 194, 'Chatter is a feature of it.', 232.771, 234.981, NULL),
  (74021, 194, 'We all have the capacity
to experience it at times.', 235.023, 238.693, NULL),
  (74022, 194, 'It also happens to be', 239.652, 241.321, NULL),
  (74023, 194, 'one of the big problems
we face as a species.', 241.362, 244.574, NULL),
  (74024, 194, 'And I say this because,
if you look at what chatter does to us,', 244.574, 248.077, NULL),
  (74025, 194, 'it sinks us in three domains of life', 248.077, 250.038, NULL),
  (74026, 194, 'that I would argue everyone here
cares a great deal about.', 250.079, 253.416, NULL),
  (74027, 194, 'One thing that chatter does,', 254.042, 255.418, NULL),
  (74028, 194, 'it makes it really hard
for us to think and perform.', 255.418, 258.129, NULL),
  (74029, 194, 'If you''ve ever had the experience', 258.963, 260.548, NULL),
  (74030, 194, 'of sitting down to read
a few pages in a book,', 260.590, 262.926, NULL),
  (74031, 194, 'and under oath, you would swear to a judge', 262.967, 265.094, NULL),
  (74032, 194, 'that you have read the words
on the screen or page,', 265.094, 268.097, NULL),
  (74033, 194, 'but you get to the end
of the section, the chapter,', 268.097, 271.184, NULL),
  (74034, 194, 'and you don''t remember
a damn thing that you''ve read,', 271.184, 273.853, NULL),
  (74035, 194, 'you''ve experienced one way
that chatter undermines us.', 273.895, 276.439, NULL),
  (74036, 194, 'It consumes our attention,
leaving very little left over', 276.439, 280.026, NULL),
  (74037, 194, 'to do the things that we often
want and need to do.', 280.026, 283.363, NULL),
  (74038, 194, 'Chatter also creates friction
in our relationships with other people,', 283.404, 286.825, NULL),
  (74039, 194, 'because when we experience chatter,', 286.866, 289.285, NULL),
  (74040, 194, 'we''re often highly motivated
to share its glory with those around us.', 289.327, 293.998, NULL),
  (74041, 194, 'What I mean by that is we often
want to talk about our chatter,', 293.998, 297.085, NULL),
  (74042, 194, 'so we find someone to talk to,', 297.085, 298.878, NULL),
  (74043, 194, 'and then, we keep on talking,
over and over again.', 298.920, 302.715, NULL),
  (74044, 194, 'This can have a really sad consequence', 303.466, 307.095, NULL),
  (74045, 194, 'of pushing away people
who genuinely care about us,', 307.136, 310.139, NULL),
  (74046, 194, 'because there''s only so much
that they can endure', 310.181, 313.309, NULL),
  (74047, 194, 'before we start to bring them down.', 313.351, 315.645, NULL),
  (74048, 194, 'Then there''s our health.', 315.645, 317.313, NULL),
  (74049, 194, 'So chatter helps explain
how stress gets under our skin', 317.313, 321.359, NULL),
  (74050, 194, 'to impact our physical health,', 321.359, 322.861, NULL),
  (74051, 194, 'because what it does
is it prolongs our stress response.', 322.902, 326.865, NULL),
  (74052, 194, 'And that creates a wear and tear
in our body that is physically damaging,', 326.865, 331.035, NULL),
  (74053, 194, 'predicts things like problems
of cardiovascular disease, inflammation,', 331.035, 334.622, NULL),
  (74054, 194, 'even certain forms of cancer.', 334.664, 336.541, NULL),
  (74055, 194, 'Now when people hear about these findings,', 337.458, 339.502, NULL),
  (74056, 194, 'the question they often ask me is:
“How can I silence this inner voice?', 339.502, 342.839, NULL),
  (74057, 194, 'Just shut it up."', 342.839, 344.507, NULL),
  (74058, 194, 'And I don’t think this is the best
question to be asking.', 344.507, 348.678, NULL),
  (74059, 194, 'Because your inner voice
is a remarkable tool.', 348.720, 352.140, NULL),
  (74060, 194, 'We don''t want to get rid of that tool.', 352.140, 354.017, NULL),
  (74061, 194, 'What we want to figure out
is how to harness it.', 354.058, 356.311, NULL),
  (74062, 194, 'And this is where the really,
really good news comes into play.', 356.311, 360.064, NULL),
  (74063, 194, 'This is precisely the question
that scientists like myself', 360.106, 363.109, NULL),
  (74064, 194, 'have been trying to answer
for a few decades now,', 363.151, 366.195, NULL),
  (74065, 194, 'and we have learned a lot
about the science-based tools', 366.237, 369.157, NULL),
  (74066, 194, 'that exist to do precisely this.', 369.198, 371.451, NULL),
  (74067, 194, 'Now there are many tools out there.', 371.451, 373.286, NULL),
  (74068, 194, 'I''m not going to tell you about each one,
because then we would go for 45 minutes.', 373.328, 377.540, NULL),
  (74069, 194, 'But I do want to share with you
three of my favorites.', 377.540, 380.126, NULL),
  (74070, 194, 'And we''re going to start with language.', 380.168, 382.670, NULL),
  (74071, 194, 'Right before Malala Yousafzai', 382.712, 384.756, NULL),
  (74072, 194, 'became the youngest person
to ever win the Nobel Peace Prize,', 384.756, 387.675, NULL),
  (74073, 194, 'for advocating for the rights
of young girls to receive an education,', 387.717, 391.679, NULL),
  (74074, 194, 'She was invited onto "The Daily
Show" with Jon Stewart', 391.679, 394.682, NULL),
  (74075, 194, 'to talk about her experience.', 394.682, 396.893, NULL),
  (74076, 194, 'At one point during the interview,', 396.893, 398.686, NULL),
  (74077, 194, 'she begins to explain
what went through her head', 398.686, 402.440, NULL),
  (74078, 194, 'when she first discovered that the Taliban
were plotting to kill her.', 402.440, 407.195, NULL),
  (74079, 194, 'I want to present to you
a quote right here,', 407.236, 409.781, NULL),
  (74080, 194, 'of how she starts to talk
about this experience.', 409.822, 412.992, NULL),
  (74081, 194, '“I used to think that the Talib
would come and he would just kill me ...”', 412.992, 416.788, NULL),
  (74082, 194, 'Nothing particularly
out of the ordinary here.', 416.788, 418.998, NULL),
  (74083, 194, 'She''s talking to herself
in the first person,', 419.040, 421.209, NULL),
  (74084, 194, 'the way we typically think
about our lives.', 421.209, 424.128, NULL),
  (74085, 194, 'But the moment she gets
to this part of the experience,', 424.629, 427.465, NULL),
  (74086, 194, '"The Taliban, they''re on my doorstep,"
"they''re coming to get me."', 427.465, 431.427, NULL),
  (74087, 194, 'It''s what is arguably the climax,', 431.427, 433.137, NULL),
  (74088, 194, 'the most stressful, chatter-provoking
event you can imagine.', 433.137, 436.557, NULL),
  (74089, 194, 'Once she gets to that part,
she does something kind of strange.', 436.599, 441.020, NULL),
  (74090, 194, 'I''m going to show you another quote,', 441.062, 442.814, NULL),
  (74091, 194, 'and I want you to look at what she says.', 442.855, 444.774, NULL),
  (74092, 194, '"I asked myself,
''What would you do, Malala?''', 444.816, 447.026, NULL),
  (74093, 194, 'Then I would reply to myself,
''Malala, just take a shoe and hit him.''', 447.026, 451.364, NULL),
  (74094, 194, 'But then I said, ''If you hit
a Talib with your shoe,', 451.406, 454.117, NULL),
  (74095, 194, 'then there would be no difference
between you and the Talib.’”', 454.158, 457.120, NULL),
  (74096, 194, 'So she starts off in the first person,
but then she switches.', 457.161, 460.039, NULL),
  (74097, 194, 'She''s coaching herself.', 460.039, 461.958, NULL),
  (74098, 194, 'She''s giving herself advice
like she would someone else,', 461.958, 465.545, NULL),
  (74099, 194, 'using her name and the word "you."', 465.586, 468.131, NULL),
  (74100, 194, 'In this instance, what Malala is doing,
she''s using a tool that we have studied.', 468.172, 472.343, NULL),
  (74101, 194, 'It is called "distanced self-talk,"', 472.385, 474.637, NULL),
  (74102, 194, 'and it is useful because we human beings
are much, much better', 474.679, 479.726, NULL),
  (74103, 194, 'at giving advice to other people
than we are taking our own advice.', 479.726, 484.022, NULL),
  (74104, 194, 'So if you''ve ever felt
like a giant hypocrite,', 484.022, 486.774, NULL),
  (74105, 194, 'once again, welcome
to the human condition.', 486.774, 488.901, NULL),
  (74106, 194, 'There''s even a name for this phenomenon.', 488.943, 491.404, NULL),
  (74107, 194, 'It''s called Solomon''s paradox,
named after the Bible''s King Solomon,', 491.446, 495.283, NULL),
  (74108, 194, 'who was famous for being able
to give great advice to other people,', 495.324, 499.537, NULL),
  (74109, 194, 'but when it came to his own affairs,
he stumbled mightily.', 499.579, 502.707, NULL),
  (74110, 194, 'Using your own name and "you"
shifts your perspective.', 502.707, 505.418, NULL),
  (74111, 194, 'It gets you to relate to yourself', 505.460, 507.128, NULL),
  (74112, 194, 'like you were giving advice
to someone else,', 507.128, 509.422, NULL),
  (74113, 194, 'and that makes it much, much easier for us
to wisely work through our problems.', 509.464, 514.552, NULL),
  (74114, 194, 'Another tool you can use
to manage your chatter is other people.', 514.594, 518.723, NULL),
  (74115, 194, 'But you have to be really careful
about who you go to for chatter support.', 518.765, 523.561, NULL),
  (74116, 194, 'Many people think that the best way
to help someone else', 523.561, 527.106, NULL),
  (74117, 194, 'is to let them vent their emotions,', 527.106, 530.068, NULL),
  (74118, 194, 'but venting doesn''t help us
work through our chatter.', 530.109, 533.529, NULL),
  (74119, 194, 'I want to repeat that again,
because it''s a really important take-home.', 533.529, 536.949, NULL),
  (74120, 194, 'Venting doesn''t help us
work through our chatter.', 536.991, 539.410, NULL),
  (74121, 194, 'Venting is really useful', 539.452, 541.120, NULL),
  (74122, 194, 'for strengthening the friendship
and relational bonds between people.', 541.120, 545.124, NULL),
  (74123, 194, 'It is good to know that someone''s there,', 545.124, 547.168, NULL),
  (74124, 194, 'they''re willing to take the time
to listen and empathize with you.', 547.210, 550.755, NULL),
  (74125, 194, 'But if all you do is vent about a problem,
you leave that conversation,', 551.172, 555.343, NULL),
  (74126, 194, 'you feel great about the person
you just spoke to,', 555.343, 557.804, NULL),
  (74127, 194, 'but the chatter is still churning', 557.845, 559.472, NULL),
  (74128, 194, 'because you haven''t done anything
to actually address it.', 559.514, 562.809, NULL),
  (74129, 194, 'The best kinds of conversations
with other people do two things.', 562.850, 566.771, NULL),
  (74130, 194, 'One, the person you''re talking to
does let you express your emotions.', 566.813, 570.399, NULL),
  (74131, 194, 'It is important for them
to empathize with you', 570.399, 572.693, NULL),
  (74132, 194, 'and validate what you''re going through.', 572.693, 574.904, NULL),
  (74133, 194, 'But then, once you''ve had an opportunity
to share your feelings,', 574.946, 578.533, NULL),
  (74134, 194, 'they ideally start working with you
to broaden your perspective.', 578.574, 582.370, NULL),
  (74135, 194, 'They''re in an ideal position
to help you do that,', 582.411, 584.789, NULL),
  (74136, 194, 'because the problem
isn''t happening to them.', 584.789, 587.125, NULL),
  (74137, 194, 'So think really carefully
about who your chatter advisors are.', 587.166, 590.920, NULL),
  (74138, 194, 'They should be people
who both listen and advise.', 590.920, 594.382, NULL),
  (74139, 194, 'That brings me to my third and final tool
that I want to share with you.', 594.382, 597.844, NULL),
  (74140, 194, 'It''s my favorite.', 597.885, 599.095, NULL),
  (74141, 194, 'It''s experiencing awe.', 599.137, 601.472, NULL),
  (74142, 194, 'About 10 years ago,', 602.181, 603.349, NULL),
  (74143, 194, 'scientists at Berkeley tracked a group
of military veterans and first responders', 603.391, 607.353, NULL),
  (74144, 194, 'as they paddled down
Utah''s majestic Green River.', 607.395, 611.190, NULL),
  (74145, 194, 'They measured participants'' levels
of PTSD and stress,', 611.232, 615.236, NULL),
  (74146, 194, 'mental states that are
infused with chatter,', 615.236, 618.239, NULL),
  (74147, 194, 'both before and after the rafting trip.', 618.281, 620.324, NULL),
  (74148, 194, 'Not surprisingly, they found
that most of the participants,', 621.284, 624.495, NULL),
  (74149, 194, 'their stress and PTSD levels declined', 624.495, 626.956, NULL),
  (74150, 194, 'from the beginning
to the end of the experiment.', 626.956, 629.667, NULL),
  (74151, 194, 'But what was surprising was the factor', 629.667, 632.170, NULL),
  (74152, 194, 'that predicted those declines
in PTSD and stress.', 632.170, 636.132, NULL),
  (74153, 194, 'It was participants'' experience of awe.', 636.132, 639.218, NULL),
  (74154, 194, 'Awe is an emotion we experience', 639.260, 640.761, NULL),
  (74155, 194, 'when we are in the presence
of something vast and indescribable.', 640.803, 644.265, NULL),
  (74156, 194, 'Lots of people get it
from an amazing sunset.', 644.265, 647.393, NULL),
  (74157, 194, 'I''m a science geek,', 647.435, 649.020, NULL),
  (74158, 194, 'so I get it when I contemplate
outer space and interplanetary travel.', 649.061, 653.941, NULL),
  (74159, 194, 'We have an SUV on Mars right now,
sending us footage back of that terrain --', 653.983, 658.196, NULL),
  (74160, 194, 'that is awe-inspiring to me.', 658.237, 660.531, NULL),
  (74161, 194, 'When we experience this emotion of awe,', 660.531, 662.658, NULL),
  (74162, 194, 'it leads to what we call
a shrinking of the self.', 662.700, 665.161, NULL),
  (74163, 194, 'We feel smaller when we''re contemplating
something vast and indescribable,', 665.203, 670.499, NULL),
  (74164, 194, 'and when we feel smaller,
so does our chatter.', 670.499, 673.628, NULL),
  (74165, 194, 'I want to wrap things up
by sharing with you', 674.462, 676.964, NULL),
  (74166, 194, 'a set of observations about our,
at times, messy emotional lives', 676.964, 681.010, NULL),
  (74167, 194, 'that I find myself
thinking about quite a bit.', 681.010, 684.972, NULL),
  (74168, 194, 'And every time I do, it fills me
with both dread, and I find it inspiring.', 685.014, 690.811, NULL),
  (74169, 194, 'Between 8,000-10,000 years ago,', 691.145, 693.147, NULL),
  (74170, 194, 'our ancestors invented
the first surgical technique.', 693.189, 697.235, NULL),
  (74171, 194, 'Its name was trepanation,', 697.235, 698.903, NULL),
  (74172, 194, 'and what it involved doing
was drilling holes in people''s skulls.', 698.903, 703.241, NULL),
  (74173, 194, 'One of the reasons why this technique
was believed to be used', 703.241, 706.869, NULL),
  (74174, 194, 'was to help people
manage their emotions --', 706.911, 709.705, NULL),
  (74175, 194, 'big, dysregulated emotional responses.', 709.705, 712.416, NULL),
  (74176, 194, 'Let the evil spirits out.', 712.458, 714.627, NULL),
  (74177, 194, 'Fast-forward to 1949.', 714.627, 716.545, NULL),
  (74178, 194, 'A Portuguese physician
wins the Nobel Prize', 716.545, 720.258, NULL),
  (74179, 194, 'for another emotion
regulation intervention.', 720.299, 723.552, NULL),
  (74180, 194, 'This one''s name?', 723.552, 725.054, NULL),
  (74181, 194, 'The frontal lobotomy.', 725.096, 727.431, NULL),
  (74182, 194, 'We have come a long way, thankfully,
from carving holes in people''s heads', 727.473, 733.729, NULL),
  (74183, 194, 'and sticking ice picks
in our frontal cortices', 733.771, 736.524, NULL),
  (74184, 194, 'to provide people with emotional relief.', 736.524, 738.526, NULL),
  (74185, 194, 'Our toolbox of science-based skills
is vastly improved.', 738.526, 743.823, NULL),
  (74186, 194, 'What we need to do a better job doing
is using these tools in our lives', 744.407, 748.411, NULL),
  (74187, 194, 'and sharing them with other people.', 748.452, 750.496, NULL),
  (74188, 194, 'We spend enormous amounts of resources', 750.496, 753.874, NULL),
  (74189, 194, 'teaching ourselves how to communicate
more effectively with other people.', 753.916, 758.212, NULL),
  (74190, 194, 'What we need to do is devote
an equivalent amount of resources', 758.587, 762.258, NULL),
  (74191, 194, 'to teaching ourselves
how to communicate more effectively', 762.258, 765.594, NULL),
  (74192, 194, 'with ourselves.', 765.594, 766.971, NULL),
  (74193, 194, 'Thank you.', 767.013, 768.222, NULL),
  (74194, 194, '(Cheers and applause)', 768.222, 772.268, NULL),
  (74195, 195, 'I''ve been feeling a lot of panic
and fear about this talk.', 4.201, 10.241, NULL),
  (74196, 195, 'And not just for the normal reasons
of public speaking,', 11.509, 14.612, NULL),
  (74197, 195, 'although that''s there, too.', 14.645, 16.147, NULL),
  (74198, 195, 'But it''s also because I want
to say something meaningful,', 16.814, 21.285, NULL),
  (74199, 195, 'and I''ve been overwhelmed by the enormity', 21.318, 24.388, NULL),
  (74200, 195, 'of what is happening right now.', 24.422, 26.490, NULL),
  (74201, 195, 'And there''s a particular
set of circumstances', 27.758, 30.294, NULL),
  (74202, 195, 'which have also been feeding
into my confusion and denial.', 30.327, 34.899, NULL),
  (74203, 195, 'And that is because the last time
that I stood on this stage,', 36.467, 41.372, NULL),
  (74204, 195, 'it led to a three-year legal battle,', 41.405, 45.376, NULL),
  (74205, 195, 'culminated in London''s High Court,', 45.409, 49.313, NULL),
  (74206, 195, 'in which it felt
like I was on trial for my life,', 49.346, 52.750, NULL),
