  (74467, 195, 'I came here, and I called out
the gods of Silicon Valley.', 925.722, 930.427, NULL),
  (74468, 195, 'I was wrong.', 931.895, 933.063, NULL),
  (74469, 195, 'Sam Altman, Mark Zuckerberg, Elon Musk,', 934.230, 939.369, NULL),
  (74470, 195, 'you are not gods.', 939.402, 941.671, NULL),
  (74471, 195, 'You are men, and you are careless.', 941.705, 944.140, NULL),
  (74472, 195, '(Applause and cheers)', 945.542, 952.449, NULL),
  (74473, 195, 'You think that by allying
yourself with an autocrat', 953.450, 957.520, NULL),
  (74474, 195, 'you will be protected.', 957.554, 959.656, NULL),
  (74475, 195, 'That''s not how history works.', 959.656, 961.591, NULL),
  (74476, 195, 'It''s not even how oligarchy works.', 961.624, 964.060, NULL),
  (74477, 195, 'This is Mikhail Khodorkovsky.', 964.060, 966.196, NULL),
  (74478, 195, 'He was an oligarch
until he was sent to Siberia,', 966.229, 970.000, NULL),
  (74479, 195, 'to prison for 10 years,', 970.033, 972.102, NULL),
  (74480, 195, 'after Putin tired of him.', 972.135, 973.970, NULL),
  (74481, 195, 'You are sucking up to a tyrant ...', 975.372, 978.241, NULL),
  (74482, 195, 'who is trying to destroy the laws', 980.577, 982.712, NULL),
  (74483, 195, 'who made your businesses possible.', 982.712, 985.115, NULL),
  (74484, 195, 'You are collaborators.', 986.716, 988.618, NULL),
  (74485, 195, 'You are complicit in a regime
of fear and cruelty.', 989.819, 995.058, NULL),
  (74486, 195, 'But the rest of us,', 996.259, 997.994, NULL),
  (74487, 195, 'we all here, we have a choice.', 998.028, 1001.464, NULL),
  (74488, 195, 'I chose to come back to TED', 1003.767, 1007.203, NULL),
  (74489, 195, 'because I''m reclaiming my story, my words.', 1007.237, 1012.575, NULL),
  (74490, 195, '(Cheers and applause) ', 1012.675, 1019.682, NULL),
  (74491, 195, 'We are not powerless.', 1023.553, 1026.823, NULL),
  (74492, 195, 'The 30,000 people who supported me', 1027.924, 1031.828, NULL),
  (74493, 195, 'proved that -- we are not powerless.', 1031.861, 1035.265, NULL),
  (74494, 195, 'Because we know who we are,
and we know what we stand for.', 1035.999, 1039.602, NULL),
  (74495, 195, 'And my question to Silicon Valley is,', 1040.503, 1043.973, NULL),
  (74496, 195, 'do you?', 1043.973, 1045.141, NULL),
  (74497, 195, 'Thank you.', 1046.810, 1047.977, NULL),
  (74498, 195, '(Cheers and applause)', 1048.011, 1054.951, NULL),
  (74499, 196, 'You are a senior military officer', 3.934, 6.837, NULL),
  (74500, 196, 'and you''ve just received a chilling
message on social media.', 6.871, 10.708, NULL),
  (74501, 196, 'Four of your soldiers have been taken,', 11.776, 14.478, NULL),
  (74502, 196, 'and if demands are not met
in the next ten minutes,', 14.478, 17.248, NULL),
  (74503, 196, 'they will be executed.', 17.281, 18.949, NULL),
  (74504, 196, 'All you have to go on
is this grainy photo,', 19.884, 22.887, NULL),
  (74505, 196, 'and you don''t have the time to figure out', 22.920, 24.889, NULL),
  (74506, 196, 'if four of your soldiers
are, in fact, missing.', 24.889, 27.558, NULL),
  (74507, 196, 'What''s your first move?', 27.591, 29.293, NULL),
  (74508, 196, 'If I may be so bold,', 30.327, 32.096, NULL),
  (74509, 196, 'your first move is to contact
somebody like me and my team.', 32.129, 36.167, NULL),
  (74510, 196, 'I am by training an applied mathematician
and computer scientist.', 37.134, 40.404, NULL),
  (74511, 196, 'And I know that seems like a very
strange first call at a moment like this,', 40.438, 44.542, NULL),
  (74512, 196, 'but I have spent the last 30 years
developing technologies', 44.542, 48.579, NULL),
  (74513, 196, 'to analyze and authenticate
digital images and digital videos.', 48.579, 53.617, NULL),
  (74514, 196, 'Along the way,', 54.752, 55.920, NULL),
  (74515, 196, 'we''ve worked with journalists,
with courts and with governments', 55.953, 59.256, NULL),
  (74516, 196, 'on a range of cases', 59.290, 61.025, NULL),
  (74517, 196, 'from a damning photo of a cheating spouse,', 61.058, 65.029, NULL),
  (74518, 196, 'gut-wrenching images of child abuse,', 65.062, 68.399, NULL),
  (74519, 196, 'photographic evidence
in a capital murder case,', 68.432, 71.702, NULL),
  (74520, 196, 'and of course, things
that we just can''t talk about.', 71.735, 74.638, NULL),
  (74521, 196, 'It used to be a case would come
across my desk once a month.', 76.006, 79.877, NULL),
  (74522, 196, 'And then it was once a week.', 81.045, 83.114, NULL),
  (74523, 196, 'Now, it''s almost every day.', 83.147, 85.916, NULL),
  (74524, 196, 'And the reason for this escalation
is a combination of things.', 86.951, 90.121, NULL),
  (74525, 196, 'One, generative AI.', 90.154, 93.057, NULL),
  (74526, 196, 'We now have the ability to create images', 93.057, 94.992, NULL),
  (74527, 196, 'that are almost
indistinguishable from reality.', 95.025, 98.863, NULL),
  (74528, 196, 'Two, social media dominates the world', 98.863, 103.000, NULL),
  (74529, 196, 'and is largely unregulated', 103.033, 105.102, NULL),
  (74530, 196, 'and actively promotes
and amplifies lies and conspiracies', 105.136, 109.907, NULL),
  (74531, 196, 'over the truth.', 109.940, 111.142, NULL),
  (74532, 196, 'And collectively, this means
that it is becoming harder and harder', 111.442, 115.412, NULL),
  (74533, 196, 'to believe anything
that we read, see or hear online.', 115.446, 119.717, NULL),
  (74534, 196, 'I contend that we are
in a global war for truth', 120.918, 126.223, NULL),
  (74535, 196, 'with profound consequences
for individuals,', 126.257, 129.827, NULL),
  (74536, 196, 'for institutions, for societies,
and for democracies.', 129.860, 133.297, NULL),
  (74537, 196, 'And I''d like to spend
a little time talking today', 134.431, 137.168, NULL),
  (74538, 196, 'about what my team and I are doing', 137.201, 139.570, NULL),
  (74539, 196, 'to try to return some of that trust
to our online world', 139.603, 142.873, NULL),
  (74540, 196, 'and in turn, our offline world.', 142.907, 144.675, NULL),
  (74541, 196, 'For 200 years, it seemed reasonable
to trust photographs.', 146.377, 149.980, NULL),
  (74542, 196, 'But even in the mid 1800s,', 150.948, 153.584, NULL),
  (74543, 196, 'it turns out the Victorians
had a sense of humor.', 153.584, 156.020, NULL),
  (74544, 196, 'They manipulated images.', 156.053, 157.555, NULL),
  (74545, 196, 'Or you could alter history.', 158.189, 160.558, NULL),
  (74546, 196, 'If you fell out of favor
with Stalin, for example,', 160.591, 163.093, NULL),
  (74547, 196, 'you may be airbrushed
out of the history books.', 163.093, 166.497, NULL),
  (74548, 196, 'But then, in the turn of the millennium,', 167.398, 170.234, NULL),
  (74549, 196, 'with the rise of digital cameras', 170.234, 172.469, NULL),
  (74550, 196, 'and photo-editing software,', 172.503, 174.171, NULL),
  (74551, 196, 'it became easier and easier
to manipulate reality.', 174.205, 178.075, NULL),
  (74552, 196, 'And now, with generative AI,', 178.976, 181.645, NULL),
  (74553, 196, 'anybody can create any image
of anything, anywhere,', 181.679, 185.549, NULL),
  (74554, 196, 'at a touch of a button.', 185.583, 187.117, NULL),
  (74555, 196, 'From four soldiers tied up in a basement', 187.651, 192.356, NULL),
  (74556, 196, 'to a giraffe, trying
on a turtleneck sweater.', 192.389, 195.926, NULL),
  (74557, 196, '(Laughter)', 195.926, 197.094, NULL),
  (74558, 196, 'It''s not fun and games, of course,', 200.397, 202.066, NULL),
  (74559, 196, 'because generative AI is being used
to supercharge past threats', 202.099, 206.770, NULL),
  (74560, 196, 'and create entirely new ones.', 206.804, 208.405, NULL),
  (74561, 196, 'The creation of nudes
of real women and children', 209.240, 212.343, NULL),
  (74562, 196, 'used to humiliate or extort them.', 212.376, 214.478, NULL),
  (74563, 196, 'Fake videos of doctors promoting
bogus cures for serious illnesses.', 215.813, 220.451, NULL),
  (74564, 196, 'A Fortune 500 company losing
tens of millions of dollars', 222.586, 226.657, NULL),
  (74565, 196, 'because an AI impersonator
of their CEO infiltrated a video call.', 226.657, 231.795, NULL),
  (74566, 196, 'Those threats are real,', 232.463, 233.931, NULL),
  (74567, 196, 'they are here, and we are all vulnerable.', 233.964, 237.101, NULL),
  (74568, 196, 'Before we talk about how
we would analyze this image', 238.602, 241.038, NULL),
  (74569, 196, 'to determine if it''s real or not,', 241.038, 242.640, NULL),
  (74570, 196, 'it''s useful to understand
how generative AI works.', 242.673, 245.309, NULL),
  (74571, 196, 'Starting with billions of images
with a descriptive caption like this,', 246.110, 251.615, NULL),
  (74572, 196, 'each image is degraded until
nothing but visual noise is left.', 251.649, 256.287, NULL),
  (74573, 196, 'A random array of pixels.', 256.320, 257.755, NULL),
  (74574, 196, 'And then the AI model learns
how to reverse that process', 258.922, 264.695, NULL),
  (74575, 196, 'by essentially turning that noise', 264.695, 267.197, NULL),
  (74576, 196, 'back into the original image.', 267.231, 269.233, NULL),
  (74577, 196, 'And when this process is done,
not once, not twice,', 270.034, 273.404, NULL),
  (74578, 196, 'but billions of times
on a diverse set of images,', 273.437, 277.508, NULL),
  (74579, 196, 'the machine has learned
how to convert noise', 277.541, 280.544, NULL),
  (74580, 196, 'into an image that is semantically
consistent with anything you type.', 280.577, 284.315, NULL),
  (74581, 196, 'And it''s incredible.', 285.382, 286.784, NULL),
  (74582, 196, 'But it is decidedly not
how a natural photograph is taken,', 287.318, 291.355, NULL),
  (74583, 196, 'which is the result of converting
light that strikes an electronic sensor', 291.355, 294.958, NULL),
  (74584, 196, 'into a digital representation.', 294.958, 296.627, NULL),
  (74585, 196, 'And so one of the first things
we like to look at', 297.294, 299.596, NULL),
  (74586, 196, 'is whether the residual noise in an image', 299.630, 302.132, NULL),
  (74587, 196, 'looks more like a natural image', 302.132, 304.101, NULL),
  (74588, 196, 'or an AI-generated image.', 304.134, 305.703, NULL),
  (74589, 196, 'Here, for example,
is our real dog and our AI dog.', 306.737, 309.907, NULL),
  (74590, 196, 'And here is the residual noise
that I''ve extracted.', 310.507, 313.510, NULL),
  (74591, 196, 'And if you look at this,', 314.311, 315.479, NULL),
  (74592, 196, 'it''s not at all obvious that there''s
any difference between those two patterns.', 315.479, 319.216, NULL),
  (74593, 196, 'But here, in this
visualization of the noise,', 319.249, 321.618, NULL),
  (74594, 196, 'you can see a decidedly different pattern', 321.652, 324.088, NULL),
  (74595, 196, 'between the natural and the artificial.', 324.121, 326.690, NULL),
  (74596, 196, 'Those star-like patterns
are a telltale sign of generative AI.', 326.724, 331.462, NULL),
  (74597, 196, 'Now, for the mathematicians
and the physicists in the audience,', 331.995, 335.132, NULL),
  (74598, 196, 'that is the magnitude of the Fourier
transform of the noise residual.', 335.165, 338.602, NULL),
  (74599, 196, 'For everybody else,
that detail doesn''t matter,', 338.635, 340.871, NULL),
  (74600, 196, 'but you definitely should have taken
more math in college.', 340.904, 343.640, NULL),
  (74601, 196, '(Laughter)', 343.674, 345.008, NULL),
  (74602, 196, 'Professors can''t help themselves.', 345.042, 347.010, NULL),
  (74603, 196, 'So let''s apply this analysis
to this image.', 347.878, 350.948, NULL),
  (74604, 196, 'Here''s the noise residual
that I''ve extracted.', 350.981, 353.250, NULL),
  (74605, 196, 'And there is that star-like pattern
that you see in the bottom right.', 353.250, 356.720, NULL),
  (74606, 196, 'Our first suggestion
that something may be wrong here.', 356.754, 360.791, NULL),
  (74607, 196, 'But no forensic technique is perfect.', 361.358, 363.627, NULL),
  (74608, 196, 'And so you don''t stop after one thing,', 363.660, 365.496, NULL),
  (74609, 196, 'you keep going.', 365.529, 366.930, NULL),
  (74610, 196, 'So let''s go on to our next one,
the vanishing points.', 366.964, 370.134, NULL),
  (74611, 196, 'If you image parallel lines
in the physical world,', 370.501, 373.504, NULL),
  (74612, 196, 'they will converge to a single point,
what''s called the vanishing point.', 373.504, 377.107, NULL),
  (74613, 196, 'A good intuition for that,
the railroad tracks.', 377.441, 380.177, NULL),
  (74614, 196, 'When I took this photo, the railroad
tracks are obviously parallel,', 380.210, 383.380, NULL),
  (74615, 196, 'but you can see that they narrow
as they recede away from me', 383.414, 387.217, NULL),
  (74616, 196, 'and intersect at a single vanishing point.', 387.217, 389.219, NULL),
  (74617, 196, 'This is a phenomenon that artists
have known for centuries.', 389.253, 392.389, NULL),
  (74618, 196, 'But here''s the great thing.', 392.423, 393.991, NULL),
  (74619, 196, 'AI doesn''t know this.', 393.991, 395.759, NULL),
  (74620, 196, 'Because AI is fundamentally,
as I just described,', 396.260, 399.129, NULL),
  (74621, 196, 'a statistical process.', 399.163, 401.031, NULL),
  (74622, 196, 'It doesn''t understand the physical world,
the geometry and the physics.', 401.064, 404.501, NULL),
  (74623, 196, 'So if we can find physical
and geometric anomalies,', 404.501, 407.404, NULL),
  (74624, 196, 'we can find evidence
of manipulation or generation.', 407.438, 411.308, NULL),
  (74625, 196, 'Here in this image,
I''ve annotated four parallel lines', 412.309, 415.112, NULL),
  (74626, 196, 'on the parallel sides of the wall
in our basement photo,', 415.145, 418.248, NULL),
  (74627, 196, 'and you can see a lack
of a coherent vanishing point.', 418.248, 422.352, NULL),
  (74628, 196, 'That suggests a physically
implausible scene.', 422.352, 425.656, NULL),
  (74629, 196, 'Evidence number two.', 426.123, 428.125, NULL),
  (74630, 196, 'Alright, what else can we learn?', 428.826, 430.527, NULL),
  (74631, 196, 'Surprisingly, shadows have a lot
in common with vanishing points.', 430.928, 434.364, NULL),
  (74632, 196, 'Here, what I''ve done
is I''ve annotated a point on a shadow', 434.765, 438.469, NULL),
  (74633, 196, 'with the corresponding part
on the bottom of the rail', 438.469, 441.171, NULL),
  (74634, 196, 'that is casting that shadow.', 441.171, 442.773, NULL),
  (74635, 196, 'And I''ve extended those lines outwards.', 442.773, 445.242, NULL),
  (74636, 196, 'And they intersect,
not at a vanishing point,', 445.576, 448.712, NULL),
  (74637, 196, 'but at the light
that is casting that shadow.', 448.712, 451.415, NULL),
  (74638, 196, 'And again, this is a physical phenomena
that you expect in natural images.', 452.749, 456.553, NULL),
  (74639, 196, 'And because AI fundamentally
doesn''t model the physics', 456.587, 459.756, NULL),
  (74640, 196, 'and the geometry of the world,', 459.790, 461.258, NULL),
  (74641, 196, 'it tends to violate these physics.', 461.258, 463.861, NULL),
  (74642, 196, 'Let''s apply this analysis to our image.', 464.895, 466.964, NULL),
  (74643, 196, 'Here I''ve annotated
four shadows on the bottom', 467.831, 470.467, NULL),
  (74644, 196, 'from the soldiers'' shadows to their legs.', 470.467, 473.437, NULL),
  (74645, 196, 'And you can see that the lines
aren''t even close to intersecting.', 473.437, 477.007, NULL),
  (74646, 196, 'Not one, not two, but three anomalies.', 477.407, 481.778, NULL),
  (74647, 196, 'We now have a very good indication
that this image is not authentic.', 482.179, 486.917, NULL),
  (74648, 196, 'The most important thing
I want you to take away from this', 488.919, 492.055, NULL),
  (74649, 196, 'is that while it may not be easy,', 492.055, 494.825, NULL),
  (74650, 196, 'it is possible to distinguish
what is real from what is fake.', 494.858, 499.329, NULL),
  (74651, 196, 'I think this image is a bit of a metaphor
for how a lot of us feel.', 500.464, 505.469, NULL),
  (74652, 196, 'We feel like hostages.', 506.904, 508.205, NULL),
  (74653, 196, 'We don''t know what to trust anymore.', 509.540, 511.608, NULL),
  (74654, 196, 'We don''t know what is real.', 511.608, 513.176, NULL),
  (74655, 196, 'What is fake.', 513.210, 514.511, NULL),
  (74656, 196, 'But we don''t have to be hostages.', 515.846, 518.048, NULL),
  (74657, 196, 'We don''t have to succumb
to the worst human instincts', 518.782, 522.319, NULL),
  (74658, 196, 'that pollute our online communities.', 522.352, 525.322, NULL),
  (74659, 196, 'We have agency, and we can effect change.', 525.322, 528.191, NULL),
  (74660, 196, 'Now, I can''t turn you all into digital
forensics experts in ten minutes.', 529.192, 535.198, NULL),
  (74661, 196, 'But I can leave you with a few thoughts.', 536.400, 538.869, NULL),
  (74662, 196, 'One, take comfort in knowing', 538.869, 542.039, NULL),
  (74663, 196, 'that the tools that I''ve described
and that my team and I are developing', 542.072, 545.475, NULL),
  (74664, 196, 'are being made available
to journalists, to institutions,', 545.509, 549.346, NULL),
  (74665, 196, 'to the courts to help them
tell what''s real and fake,', 549.379, 552.583, NULL),
  (74666, 196, 'which in turn helps you.', 552.583, 554.151, NULL),
  (74667, 196, 'Two, there is an international standard', 554.184, 556.954, NULL),
  (74668, 196, 'for so-called content credentials', 556.987, 559.456, NULL),
  (74669, 196, 'that can authenticate content
at the point of creation.', 559.489, 563.560, NULL),
  (74670, 196, 'As these credentials start to roll out,
they will help you, the consumer,', 563.594, 567.531, NULL),
  (74671, 196, 'figure out what is real
and what is fake online.', 567.564, 570.667, NULL),
  (74672, 196, 'And while they won''t solve
all of our problems,', 570.701, 572.970, NULL),
  (74673, 196, 'they will absolutely be part
of a larger solution.', 573.003, 576.139, NULL),
  (74674, 196, 'Three, please understand', 577.307, 580.243, NULL),
  (74675, 196, 'that social media is not a place
to get news and information.', 580.243, 585.082, NULL),
  (74676, 196, '(Applause)', 585.649, 592.356, NULL),
  (74677, 196, 'It is a place that Silicon Valley
created to steal your time,', 592.389, 597.594, NULL),
  (74678, 196, 'your attention,', 597.628, 599.029, NULL),
  (74679, 196, 'by delivering you
the equivalent of junk food.', 599.062, 602.265, NULL),
  (74680, 196, 'And like -- thank you.', 603.300, 604.968, NULL),
  (74681, 196, '(Applause)', 605.002, 606.903, NULL),
  (74682, 196, 'And like any bad habit, you should quit.', 606.937, 609.773, NULL),
  (74683, 196, '(Laughter)', 609.806, 610.941, NULL),
  (74684, 196, 'And if you can''t quit,', 610.974, 612.676, NULL),
  (74685, 196, 'at least do not let this be
your primary source of information,', 612.709, 615.779, NULL),
  (74686, 196, 'because it is simply too riddled
with lies and conspiracies', 615.812, 620.350, NULL),
  (74687, 196, 'and now AI slop,', 620.350, 621.752, NULL),
  (74688, 196, 'to be even close to being reliable.', 621.785, 624.121, NULL),
  (74689, 196, 'Four.', 624.788, 626.023, NULL),
  (74690, 196, 'Understand that when you share
false or misleading information,', 626.857, 630.527, NULL),
  (74691, 196, 'intentionally or not,
you''re all part of the problem.', 630.560, 633.463, NULL),
  (74692, 196, 'Don''t be part of the problem.', 634.498, 635.966, NULL),
  (74693, 196, 'There are serious, smart,', 635.999, 637.401, NULL),
  (74694, 196, 'hard-working journalists
and fact-checkers out there', 637.434, 639.870, NULL),
  (74695, 196, 'who work every day,', 639.903, 641.338, NULL),
  (74696, 196, 'because I talk to them every day,', 641.371, 643.140, NULL),
  (74697, 196, 'to sort out the lies from the truths.', 643.140, 645.142, NULL),
  (74698, 196, 'Take a breath before you
share information,', 645.175, 649.279, NULL),
  (74699, 196, 'and don''t deceive your friends
and your families and your colleagues,', 649.312, 652.849, NULL),
  (74700, 196, 'and further pollute the online
information ecosystem.', 652.883, 656.219, NULL),
  (74701, 196, '(Applause)', 657.421, 662.025, NULL),
  (74702, 196, 'We''re at a fork in the road.', 662.459, 664.227, NULL),
  (74703, 196, 'One path, we can keep doing
what we''ve been doing for 20 years,', 665.128, 669.199, NULL),
  (74704, 196, 'allowing technology
to rip us apart as a society,', 669.232, 673.336, NULL),
  (74705, 196, 'sowing distrust, hate, intolerance.', 673.370, 676.773, NULL),
  (74706, 196, 'Or we can change paths.', 677.908, 679.476, NULL),
  (74707, 196, 'We can find a new way to leverage
the power of technology to work for us', 679.943, 684.881, NULL),
  (74708, 196, 'and with us, and not against us.', 684.915, 687.484, NULL),
  (74709, 196, 'That choice is entirely ours.', 688.018, 689.753, NULL),
  (74710, 196, 'Thank you.', 690.153, 691.421, NULL),
  (74711, 196, '(Applause)', 691.421, 698.428, NULL),
  (74712, 196, 'Latif Nasser: We''re doing rapid-fire
questions, you ready?', 699.663, 702.399, NULL),
  (74713, 196, 'Roughly what percent of images online
do you believe to be fake?', 702.432, 705.469, NULL),
  (74714, 196, 'Hany Farid: Depends on the platform.', 706.069, 707.871, NULL),
  (74715, 196, 'Signal-to-noise ratio
is getting close to one.', 707.871, 710.040, NULL),
  (74716, 196, 'Stay off of Twitter, of X, and stay off
of everything else for that matter.', 710.040, 713.577, NULL),
  (74717, 196, 'LN: So what do you think?', 713.610, 714.811, NULL),
  (74718, 196, 'HF: I would say we''re getting
close to 50 percent.', 714.845, 717.180, NULL),
  (74719, 196, 'LN: Can you differentiate
between things that have, like,', 717.214, 720.016, NULL),
