  (84671, 205, '- The following is a conversation with Irving
Finkel, who is a scholar of ancient languages.', 0.080, 3.860, NULL),
  (84672, 205, 'He''s a curator at the British Museum for over 45 years,
and is a much admired and respected world expert.', 3.960, 11.720, NULL),
  (84673, 205, 'He''s an expert on cuneiform script and more generally, on
ancient languages like Sumerian, Akkadian, and Babylonian.', 11.780, 19.330, NULL),
  (84674, 205, 'He''s also an expert on ancient board games,
Mesopotamia magic, medicine, literature, and culture.', 19.380, 27.330, NULL),
  (84675, 205, 'I should also mention that both on and off the mic,
Irving was a super kind and fun person to talk to.', 27.460, 34.980, NULL),
  (84676, 205, 'He has an infectious enthusiasm for ancient history that
of course I already love, but fell in love with even more.', 35.040, 41.780, NULL),
  (84677, 205, 'This is the Lex Fridman Podcast. To support it,
please check out our sponsors in the description.', 41.800, 45.700, NULL),
  (84678, 205, 'You can also find links to contact me,
ask questions, get feedback, and so on.', 45.720, 49.600, NULL),
  (84679, 205, 'And now, dear friends,
here''s Irving Finkel.', 49.640, 56.150, NULL),
  (84680, 205, 'Where and when did writing
originate in human civilization?', 56.740, 60.580, NULL),
  (84681, 205, 'Let''s go back a few thousand years.', 60.620, 65.280, NULL),
  (84682, 205, '- The first attempts at writing that we could call
writing go back to the middle of the fourth millennium,', 65.300, 69.020, NULL),
  (84683, 205, 'say around 3500 BC, something like that.', 69.220, 76.240, NULL),
  (84684, 205, 'There were people in the Middle East, individuals
