  (106102, 213, 'please check out our sponsors in the
description, where you can also find', 30.880, 34.580, NULL),
  (106103, 213, 'links to contact me, ask
questions, give feedback, and so', 35.040, 38.920, NULL),
  (106104, 213, 'on. And now, dear friends,
here''s Michael Levin.', 39.060, 43.920, NULL),
  (106105, 213, 'You write that the central question
at the heart of your work from', 45.080, 48.860, NULL),
  (106106, 213, 'biological systems to
computational ones is, "How do', 48.880, 52.760, NULL),
  (106107, 213, 'embodied minds arise in the
physical world, and what', 52.840, 56.820, NULL),
  (106108, 213, 'determines the capabilities and
properties of those minds?" Can you', 56.860, 60.520, NULL),
  (106109, 213, 'unpack that question for us,
and maybe begin to answer it?', 60.640, 64.200, NULL),
  (106110, 213, '- Well, the fundamental tension
is in both the first-person,', 64.220, 67.840, NULL),
  (106111, 213, 'the second-person, and
third-person descriptions of mind.', 67.880, 71.320, NULL),
  (106112, 213, 'So, in third-person, we want to
understand how do we recognize', 71.360, 74.900, NULL),
  (106113, 213, 'them, and how do we know, looking out into
the world, what degree of agency there', 74.940, 78.870, NULL),
  (106114, 213, 'is, and how best to relate to the
different systems that we find.', 78.940, 82.880, NULL),
  (106115, 213, 'And are our intuitions any good when
we look at something and it looks', 82.890, 86.720, NULL),
  (106116, 213, 'really stupid and mechanical,
versus it really looks like there''s', 86.760, 90.250, NULL),
  (106117, 213, 'something cognitive going on there? How
do we get good at recognizing them?', 90.260, 93.540, NULL),
  (106118, 213, 'Then there''s the second-person, which
is the control, and that''s both for', 94.120, 98.020, NULL),
  (106119, 213, 'engineering but also for regenerative medicine,
when you want to tell the system to do', 98.080, 101.720, NULL),
  (106120, 213, 'something, right? What kind of tools are
