  (121623, 217, 'completion." And then he goes on to explain
the matter, it concerns his basic law', 3649.196, 3653.076, NULL),
  (121624, 217, 'five, and so on, and...', 3653.156, 3654.386, NULL),
  (121625, 217, '- It''s heartbreaking. I mean,
there''s nothing more traumatic to', 3654.396, 3657.056, NULL),
  (121626, 217, 'a person who dreams of constructing
mathematics all from logic.', 3658.056, 3661.976, NULL),
  (121627, 217, 'to get a very clean, simple
contradiction. I mean, that''s just...', 3662.716, 3668.386, NULL),
  (121628, 217, '- You devote your life to this work, and
then it''s shown to be contradictory, and', 3668.396, 3673.416, NULL),
  (121629, 217, 'that must have been heartbreaking.', 3673.496, 3675.006, NULL),
  (121630, 217, '- What do you think about the Frege
project, the philosophy of logic,', 3676.676, 3680.596, NULL),
  (121631, 217, 'the dream of the power of logic-', 3680.606, 3682.376, NULL),
  (121632, 217, '- Right', 3682.496, 3682.596, NULL),
  (121633, 217, '- ... to construct a mathematical universe?', 3682.606, 3684.176, NULL),
  (121634, 217, '- So, of course, the project
of logicism did not die with', 3684.196, 3687.996, NULL),
  (121635, 217, 'Frege, and it was continued,
